(534,NULL,'When variable resistor is $0\\,\\Omega$ voltmeter reading $= 6.0\\,\\text{V}$ (1)\n\nUse of principle of potential divider **or** use of $V = IR$ (1)\n\nWhen variable resistor is $40\\,\\Omega$ voltmeter reading $= 1.2\\,\\text{V}$ (1)\n\nExample: $V = (10\\,\\Omega / 50\\,\\Omega) \\times 6\\,\\text{V} = 1.2\\,\\text{V}$','MARK_SCHEME'),
