(578,NULL,'Extended response (6 marks): up to 4 marks for indicative content (6 IC = 4, 5–4 IC = 3, 3–2 IC = 2, 1 IC = 1) and up to 2 marks for structure and lines of reasoning.\n\nIndicative content:\n\nIC1 Positive potential difference from A (to B)\n\nIC2 So there is a current (12.5 mA) in the LED\n\nIC3 Therefore LED is lit\n\nIC4 Negative potential difference from B (to C)\n\nIC5 So there is no current in the LED Or so resistance of LED is (very) high\n\nIC6 Therefore LED is not lit','MARK_SCHEME'),
(579,NULL,'Use of charge = area under the graph (1)\n\nCharge in 5 hours $= 89\\,(\\text{A h})$ (1)\n\n$90\\%$ charge is $99\\,(\\text{A h})$ so statement is not correct Or $89\\,(\\text{A h})$ is $81\\%$ charge so statement is not correct (1)\n\n[MP3 dependent on MP1]\n\nExample: $Q = 0.5(0.5 \\times 17.5) + 0.5(4.5 \\times 2.5) + (17.5 \\times 4.5) = 88.8\\,\\text{A h}$; $90\\%$ charge $= 0.9 \\times 110 = 99\\,\\text{A h}$','MARK_SCHEME'),
(580,NULL,'Use of efficiency $= \\dfrac{\\text{useful energy output}}{\\text{total energy input}}$ and conversion of kW h to J (1)\n\nUse of $\\Delta W = F\\Delta s$ (1)\n\n$F = 803\\,(\\text{N})$ (1)\n\nExample: useful energy output $= 0.85 \\times 42\\,000 \\times 3600 = 1.29\\times10^8\\,\\text{J}$; $1.29\\times10^8 = F \\times 160\\times10^3$; $F = 803\\,\\text{N}$','MARK_SCHEME'),
(581,NULL,'Use of $mg\\Delta h$ (1)\n\nUse of useful energy output = work done against frictional forces $+ \\Delta E_{\\text{grav}}$ (allow ecf from (b)(i)) Or use of $\\Delta E_{\\text{grav}}$ = reduction in work done against frictional forces (1)\n\nReduction in range $= 47\\,\\text{km}$ (1)\n\nExample: $\\Delta E_{\\text{grav}} = 1300 \\times 9.81 \\times 3000 = 3.8\\times10^7\\,\\text{J}$; $1.29\\times10^8 = 803s + 3.8\\times10^7$; $s = 113\\,\\text{km}$; reduction $= 160 - 113 = 47\\,\\text{km}$','MARK_SCHEME'),
