(625,21,4,'9',8,'STRUCTURED',3,'An electric motor takes $45.0\\,\\text{s}$ to lift a mass of $800\\,\\text{kg}$ through a vertical height of $14.0\\,\\text{m}$. The potential difference across the motor is $230\\,\\text{V}$ and the current is $13.0\\,\\text{A}$.\n\nCalculate the efficiency of the motor.',NULL,27,51,'Efficiency and power','MEDIUM',5,'[5]','0.90','PUBLISHED',NULL,'2026-10-05 18:26:14',NULL,'[347,384,515,531,594,481,483,580,486,581]','2026-10-05 18:26:35',NULL),
(626,21,4,'10(a)(i)',9,'STRUCTURED',1,'The photograph shows cars travelling on a straight section of a motorway.\n\nThe maximum speed limit on a motorway in the U.K. is $31\\,\\text{m s}^{-1}$.\n\n(a) A car is travelling along the motorway at $31\\,\\text{m s}^{-1}$. The driver sees stationary traffic $180\\,\\text{m}$ ahead. After $0.6\\,\\text{s}$ the driver reacts by applying a constant braking force that stops the car in $10\\,\\text{s}$.\n\n(i) Draw a velocity-time graph of the car\'s motion, from the instant the driver sees the stationary traffic until the car stops.',NULL,27,41,'Velocity-time graphs','EASY',6,'[6]','0.90','PUBLISHED',NULL,'2026-10-05 18:26:14',NULL,'[575,381,382,421,357,502,535,506,530,495]','2026-10-05 18:26:35',NULL),
